      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $285^\\circ=225^\\circ+60^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(285^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(225^\\circ+60^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(60^\\circ\\right)+\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
